WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.877
Treat these as guided practice rather than a checklist to rush through.

00:00:03.877 --> 00:00:08.372
Solve one task at a time, predict what Python should do,

00:00:08.372 --> 00:00:11.612
and explain your reasoning before running the code.

00:00:11.612 --> 00:00:18.482
If the result differs from the prediction, inspect intermediate values instead of immediately replacing your

00:00:18.482 --> 00:00:22.182
work. Think about where this function would appear in a larger project.

00:00:22.182 --> 00:00:30.267
Cleaning one value, calculating one metric, or validating one record can become a reusable function applied

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.862
across many rows, files, or notebooks.

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:37.622
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:43.042
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
